SpotBugs exclusions (issue #223). Each pattern is switched off for the whole code base, with the
reason below. Nothing here hides a bug class that applies: every pattern was read at each of its
sites first, and the sites that were real bugs were fixed. A new kind of finding fails the build.

EI_EXPOSE_REP, EI_EXPOSE_REP2, MS_EXPOSE_REP
    Fires on every record or class that hands out a List, Map, Set, Message or a shared ObjectMapper.
    The values are immutable by contract (copied with List.copyOf and the like in the constructor, or
    never modified after construction). Errors in that contract show up in the unit tests of the
    records, which check the copies.
SECPR
    ThreadLocalRandom is used for retry jitter and shuffling, never for tokens, keys or ids. Secrets
    come from SecureRandom.
USO (unsafe synchronization on the outer class)
    The inner Slot of ConnectionLimiter locks its outer limiter on purpose; the outer class is not
    visible outside the package.
DMI_HARDCODED_ABSOLUTE_FILENAME
    Detection of the operating system by well-known paths (/proc, /etc/os-release, /.dockerenv,
    /lib/ld-musl). They are probes, not configuration.
VA_FORMAT_STRING_USES_NEWLINE
    Console and generated files use LF on every platform on purpose (compose files, the launcher
    messages that are tested for exact text).
SECCI (command injection)
    Every ProcessBuilder here takes a fixed program and an argument list (no shell). Values from
    configuration go to arguments, never into a command string. The same sites carry a reasoned
    nosemgrep comment and are covered by CodeQL.
SECRD (regular expression DoS)
    The flagged expressions have bounded repeats ({0,61}) and are applied to short, length-checked
    input (host names, version tags, JVM flags).
SECPTI (Files.createTemp* in a configured directory), SECOPFP (permissions of extracted files)
    The directories belong to the cloud home. The extracted file mode comes from the archive and is
    cut to owner-write by SafeExtractor.
SECSQLIJDBC
    The statements of JdbcConnector are administrative statements built from validated identifiers
    (database and user names pass ConfigNames), not from request data.
SECWTM
    The cluster trust manager accepts exactly the pinned CA fingerprint of the cluster (see
    ClusterTrust); it is not an accept-all manager.
SECUSS
    PortAllocator only binds a port to see whether it is free and closes it again.
SECUHE
    The compared value is a public checksum of a file, not a secret.
ERRMSG
    The messages go to the operator's own console and log, not to a remote client.
BX_UNBOXING_IMMEDIATELY_REBOXED
    Config records use Integer / Boolean components to say "not set"; the cost is irrelevant.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <Match><Bug code="EI,EI2,MS"/></Match>
    <Match><Bug code="SECPR"/></Match>
    <Match><Bug code="USO"/></Match>
    <Match><Bug pattern="DMI_HARDCODED_ABSOLUTE_FILENAME"/></Match>
    <Match><Bug pattern="VA_FORMAT_STRING_USES_NEWLINE"/></Match>
    <Match><Bug code="SECCI,SECRD,SECPTI,SECOPFP,SECSQLIJDBC,SECWTM,SECUSS,SECUHE,ERRMSG"/></Match>
    <Match><Bug pattern="BX_UNBOXING_IMMEDIATELY_REBOXED"/></Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
